From 7afc16282eda1b426748677342ac567b524efcf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:55:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] feat(libkernel): hand guest memory to Kyty's GPU stack
 behind APS5_GPU_ENGINE=kyty

AstroHybrid: AstroBot.exe renders with Kyty's GPU stack (kyty_gpu.dll) while
AnyPS5 keeps CPU execution and the other system services.

- libc: GuestArenaDonate / GuestArenaDonateAt split a placeholder range off
  the guest arena for another owner and never hand it out again;
  GuestArenaDonated reports whether an address lies in such a range.
- libkernel: with APS5_GPU_ENGINE=kyty the game's direct and flexible
  memory calls go to kyty_gpu.dll, and munmap, mprotect, virtual queries and
  range names go there for addresses in a donated range. Unset (default):
  unchanged. APS5_GPU_ENGINE_TRACE=1 logs each forwarded map.
- libAstroHybridHost: the host callbacks kyty_gpu.dll binds (GPU event
  registration on the game's event queues and their delivery, guest range
  donation) and the SystemService HDR hooks of the replaced driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
